#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:13
#: 416c881878ec47ed8c46db8c9bc44bad
msgid "Chapter 16 — Maintenance, Drift and Link Rot"
msgstr "第 16 章 —— 维护、漂移与链接腐化"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:15
#: 2d4ec158d2e94c2599d00172884245dd
msgid "Why"
msgstr "Why —— 为什么"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:17
#: 6e39641d27244e1faf2395ae41ef97ed
msgid ""
"Chapter 14 tells you which pages changed. Chapter 15 tells you which ones "
"cannot be published as-is. This chapter tells you what to actually *do* "
"about each one. In the terms of Chapter 7a, this is Corner C3 — the three-"
"level update strategy — written out operationally."
msgstr ""
"第 14 章告诉你哪些页面变了。第 15 章告诉你其中哪些按现状无法发布。本章讲的是：对其中每一个页面，你到底要 * 干什么 * 。用第 7a "
"章的话说，这就是第 C3 角 —— 三级更新策略 —— 的运维版展开。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:23
#: a9e26da3a1f4455ea1b76b2dd0de6fde
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The LLM era has changed the economics of maintenance, but not in the "
"direction people expected. Re-embedding a repo is nearly free "
"{cite}`openai_embeddings_v3`. Regenerating a whole page with a modern LLM is"
" pennies. Neither of those is the bottleneck any more. The bottleneck is *a "
"human understanding what changed*. If the pipeline regenerates 400 pages in "
"a week, a reviewer either becomes a rubber stamp (defeating the purpose) or "
"stops reviewing (defeating the KB)."
msgstr ""
"LLM 时代改变了“维护”的经济学，但改的方向和很多人想的不一样。重新嵌入一个仓库几乎是免费的 "
"{cite}`openai_embeddings_v3`。用现代 LLM 把整页重新生成一遍也不过是几分钱。这些都不再是瓶颈。瓶颈是 * "
"一个人去理解“到底变了什么” * 。如果流水线一周重新生成 400 "
"个页面，那评审者要么变成橡皮图章（违背评审的目的），要么干脆不评审了（违背知识库的目的）。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:31
#: feac333c3ae4472593f2b1cea7b7ee6f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The three-level strategy is the author's answer to this, refined in a "
"private project-knowledge-base toolkit {cite}`fanyamin_pkb_skill` and "
"presented here as the book's canonical discipline. It has one rule that "
"matters more than the levels: **rule first, LLM second.** If a deterministic"
" rule can do the job, do not call an LLM. Every call is a page a human may "
"need to read."
msgstr ""
"三级策略就是作者对此给出的答案 —— 在一个私有的 project-knowledge-base 工具包 "
"{cite}`fanyamin_pkb_skill` 中反复打磨而来，在本书里被作为正式的纪律呈现出来。它有一条比各级本身更重要的规则： **rule "
"first, LLM second。** 如果一条确定性规则能搞定，就不要调 LLM。每一次调用，都对应一个人可能必须要去读的 diff。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:38
#: a497e5a3475e4bee80ec88b634526cf3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Link rot {cite}`kiesling2017linkrot` is the most common symptom of "
"maintenance debt and the cleanest illustration of the three levels. This "
"chapter uses it as a running example."
msgstr ""
"链接腐化 {cite}`kiesling2017linkrot` 是“维护债”最常见的症状，也是演示这三级最干净的例子。本章把它作为贯穿全章的范例。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:42
#: 2c8c21b02cb640edb444a38eed6c7cb0
msgid "What"
msgstr "What —— 是什么"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:44
#: 003fc5a5cb9644b7981d8d548788ae37
msgid "The three levels"
msgstr "三个级别"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:46
#: dacc57f702f84fe881d87811b917c6cb
msgid ""
"Every candidate page produced by Chapter 14's sync is routed to exactly one "
"of three levels by a dispatcher whose rules are deterministic. The levels "
"differ by who pays and what they spend:"
msgstr ""
"第 14 章同步产出的每个候选页面，都会被一个规则确定性的派发器精确地路由到三个级别中的某一个。各级别的差异在于“谁来买单”以及“买的是什么”："

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 0bd1108bfbb746029486aeefb4091b0a
msgid "Level"
msgstr "级别"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 2e52be2adfaa4c02b164e35b3a25073b
msgid "Who acts"
msgstr "由谁动手"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: db49c904fb2348d083c1ac8d6441bd19
msgid "Token cost"
msgstr "Token 成本"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 59646ac5e64c4a85ab1131f6f4ce0e01
msgid "When it applies"
msgstr "适用场景"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 39cf31df1bb74a7ab03bdc8d18f70d95
msgid "What the reviewer sees"
msgstr "评审者看到什么"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 17e5d8a6729b4e5fa29592f3ff83db05
msgid "**L1 Mechanical**"
msgstr "**L1 机械化**"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 10288b3ad91e4e59b3f6af7cd638a9a8
msgid "A script"
msgstr "一段脚本"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 5b58412387a149bdbea14eee180f130b
msgid "**0**"
msgstr "**0**"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 18e13c94493d4edf8352c1b9acaaecf6
msgid ""
"Change is resolvable by rule: footer-only drift, broken link to a moved "
"file, auto-generated page (`repo-map`), stamp refresh"
msgstr "变更可被规则消化：仅 footer 漂移、指向已移动文件的坏链、自动生成页（`repo-map`）、重打时间戳"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: f7f249e56f24413799abd45d430620e4
msgid "Nothing, usually; the pending marker on the footer"
msgstr "通常什么都看不到；footer 上多一个 pending 标记"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: ec5da51fee3c4b69a23ff9066a4f4852
msgid "**L2 Bounded-LLM**"
msgstr "**L2 有界 LLM**"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 0a878b1c583040b58f6b47aaf44e6421
msgid "An LLM + small context"
msgstr "一次 LLM + 小上下文"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: d5c9126e6d544734a802fd6052d34acd
msgid "1–5 k tokens"
msgstr "1–5 k tokens"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 08275004ccd045fcbdfd30fa4ad4b76c
msgid ""
"Body references something that genuinely changed; the fix is localised to a "
"paragraph or two"
msgstr "正文引用了确实发生变化的东西；修复本身局限在一两段之内"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: b30d3851ba104d0991f31a73328cbbb1
msgid "A small diff; a `pending` footer asking for approval"
msgstr "一段小 diff；一个标着 `pending`、等待批准的 footer"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 40cf374edcb1475699fa9392c53b891f
msgid "**L3 Human-led**"
msgstr "**L3 人工主导**"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: ac8e89677db0400082528c87f6b4bd68
msgid "A human; LLM copy-edits"
msgstr "人；LLM 只做文字润色"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 0ec50196bb3e495989b38b54ee9293ea
msgid "Variable"
msgstr "不确定"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: 923778186553410e9fa4cf58a408dbdf
msgid ""
"Architectural change, new ADR, security-sensitive content, or L2 repeatedly "
"fails for the same page"
msgstr "架构级变更、新的 ADR、安全敏感内容，或同一页面 L2 反复失败"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md
#: d73adb907c87418da9788591cc59992b
msgid "A real review; sometimes a new ADR"
msgstr "一次真正的评审；有时还会产出一份新的 ADR"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:56
#: cfcf228ba1334ded8db05cd78bd534f9
msgid ""
"The levels are not a menu. A page is assigned a level; it does not get to "
"pick. The rules below determine assignment."
msgstr "这三级不是一份可以点的菜单。页面是被 * 指派 * 到某一级的，不能自选。下面的规则决定指派。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:59
#: 48f30545080b4260915bdf800accf156
msgid "The dispatcher rules"
msgstr "派发器规则"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:88
#: 2111b75d9a834f31ae3c6fb6e26e8e22
msgid "Four observations are worth pausing on:"
msgstr "有四点值得停下来说："

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:90
#: e571be66e6d04dd8a7ba79569d70bda1
msgid ""
"**Policy overrides first.** Architecture pages never get an automated "
"rewrite, even if the sync thinks the change is small. Auto-generated pages "
"never get an LLM pass, even if the change is large (it is *meant* to be "
"mechanical)."
msgstr ""
"**策略级覆盖优先。** 架构页永远不会被自动重写，哪怕同步觉得这次变更很小。自动生成页也永远不会走 LLM 通道，哪怕变更很大（它 * 本来就该 * "
"是机械的）。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:94
#: 27be6af3132140459b5d524020e0b8a1
msgid ""
"**L1 is the first positive match.** The dispatcher actively tries to resolve"
" the candidate with a rule before it considers an LLM. This is where \"rule "
"first, LLM second\" becomes real code."
msgstr ""
"**L1 是第一次肯定匹配。** 派发器会主动先尝试用规则消化候选页面，再考虑 LLM。这就是“rule first, LLM "
"second”真正落成代码的地方。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:97
#: 677feb87786441caad3916a5395a38f6
msgid ""
"**L2 only fires on evidence.** The tags are the evidence — either a moved "
"entity (L-entity) or a broken link (L-link) that survived the L1 rules. An "
"L-git-only candidate with no body drift cannot reach L2."
msgstr ""
"**L2 只在有证据时才启动。** 那些标签就是证据 —— 要么是一个移动实体（L-entity），要么是一条“在 L1 "
"规则里活下来的”坏链（L-link）。一个只被 L-git 标记、正文没有漂移的候选，是到不了 L2 的。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:101
#: 78d7bbe37f1b43c0a3a2f8fa3fab314e
msgid ""
"**Fall-through is conservative.** When the rules are ambiguous, route to a "
"human. The cost of a wrong human review is an annoyance; the cost of a wrong"
" LLM rewrite is a silent trust regression."
msgstr "**兜底是保守的。** 当规则模棱两可时，交给人。错误的人类评审的代价是“麻烦”；错误的 LLM 重写的代价是“悄无声息的信任回退”。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:106
#: fe173e9a27a1427782da601be01aa1b6
msgid "What each level actually does"
msgstr "每一级到底做什么"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:108
#: 90cfadd13861454cb24a2e0cb29694e2
msgid "**L1 Mechanical** runs pure Python or shell:"
msgstr "**L1 机械化** 跑纯 Python 或 shell："

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:110
#: 904a5428ea5a4f46a85f8a54d9bcf806
msgid ""
"`L1_STAMP` updates `commit:` and `last_updated:` in the footer; leaves "
"everything else untouched."
msgstr "`L1_STAMP` 更新 footer 里的 `commit:` 和 `last_updated:`，其他一切不碰。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:112
#: fa62e4b455634259a20a57842d32c9ab
msgid ""
"`L1_FIX_LINK` rewrites one markdown link or `file:line` anchor to point at "
"the new location of the target. If the target no longer exists at all, "
"escalates to L2."
msgstr ""
"`L1_FIX_LINK` 把一条 markdown 链接或 `file:line` 锚点重写到目标的新位置。如果目标已经彻底不存在，则升级到 L2。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:115
#: 2ff8e6263ead484ba54a854c7727883c
msgid ""
"`L1_REGENERATE` re-runs the page's generator (e.g. `repo-map.md` from `git "
"ls-files`) and overwrites the body. Footer resets per the AI-always-sets-"
"pending rule — yes, even though no LLM was involved; any automated touch "
"counts."
msgstr ""
"`L1_REGENERATE` 重跑该页面的生成器（例如用 `git ls-files` 生成 `repo-map.md`）并覆盖正文。footer 按"
" “AI 总是置 pending” 的规则重置 —— 是的，即便这次完全没动 LLM；任何自动化的触碰都算。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:120
#: 6d96754708f14535a300db2a1912e392
msgid ""
"Every L1 action resets the footer: `review_status: pending`, `review_score: "
"0`, `reviewed_by:`, `updated_by: ai` (or `human` if a human ran the script)."
" The name is a convention, not a claim that a model was called."
msgstr ""
"所有 L1 动作都会重置 footer：`review_status: pending`、`review_score: "
"0`、`reviewed_by:`、`updated_by: ai`（如果是人类跑的脚本则是 `human`）。`ai` "
"这个名字是一个约定，并不主张“调了模型”。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:125
#: caa284509cdc4e37ad19e3a0fff27a39
msgid "**L2 Bounded-LLM** calls one LLM with a carefully bounded context:"
msgstr "**L2 有界 LLM** 用一个小心受限的上下文调一次 LLM："

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:127
#: f2ca92df7289475aacd53e3f96296bf9
msgid "The *current* body of the one candidate page (~2 kB)."
msgstr "该候选页面 * 当前 * 的正文（约 2 kB）。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:128
#: 7bbf675c40904c04a9da991ae5942247
msgid "The *one diff* that triggered the change (~300 B – 2 kB)."
msgstr "触发本次变更的 * 那一份 diff * （约 300 B – 2 kB）。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:129
#: f65ba4ead5394abea8d0ba8ef070f4be
msgid "The page's footer, as a reminder of C2's vocabulary."
msgstr "该页面的 footer，作为 C2 词汇表的提示。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:130
#: 29b4a615de814c92959bf832a09af655
msgid ""
"A *system prompt* that says: you may edit only the paragraphs that cite "
"things in the diff; you may not invent citations; you must leave an explicit"
" `pending` footer."
msgstr ""
"一段 * 系统提示词 * ：你只能编辑那些引用了 diff 中内容的段落；不得凭空编造引用；必须留下一个显式的 `pending` footer。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:134
#: 0cf6b31ea36f48c487b1ab5a996f7130
msgid ""
"This bounds the token cost at roughly 5 k per call, and — more importantly —"
" bounds the *scope* of the change. L2 cannot rewrite the whole page, because"
" the prompt and the context do not contain the whole page's intent. It can "
"only fix the paragraphs it was pointed at. Drift confined to one localised "
"area is exactly the case L2 exists for."
msgstr ""
"这把每次调用的 token 成本钉在大约 5 k —— 更重要的是，它钉住了变更的 * 作用域 * 。L2 "
"不能重写整页，因为提示词和上下文里本来就没有“整页的意图”。它只能修它被指向的那几段。限制在一小片局部区域的漂移，正是 L2 存在的那个场景。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:141
#: ece6d82fd47e45f2b752902d3a7356e8
msgid ""
"**L3 Human-led** is a human writing or editing, with the LLM used (at most) "
"for copy-editing passes the human explicitly invokes. Every L3 change is a "
"real review in the normal git-and-PR sense. There is no special machinery "
"here — the discipline is that the other levels *stay out* of L3's territory."
msgstr ""
"**L3 人工主导** 是人亲自来写或来改，LLM 至多被用来做“人类明确发起”的文字润色。每一次 L3 变更都是一次正常 git-and-PR "
"意义上的真正评审。这里没有什么特别的机制 —— 真正的纪律是：其他级别 * 不要踏进 * L3 的地盘。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:147
#: 90de5a176fe0410fa1838bb91caa5429
msgid "How"
msgstr "How —— 怎么做"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:149
#: ca754ec62b62499bac53736fcecf6736
msgid "Link rot as the canonical worked example"
msgstr "以链接腐化为正宗范例"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:151
#: 7a49710f61ec466586e39977e7f5f5ee
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Link rot {cite}`kiesling2017linkrot` deserves a dedicated walk-through "
"because it is the failure most readers have personally seen and because it "
"exercises all three levels in one scenario."
msgstr ""
"链接腐化 {cite}`kiesling2017linkrot` "
"值得被单独走一遍，一是因为大多数读者都亲眼见过这种失败，二是因为它在一个场景里就能把三个级别全都练到。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:155
#: 3945dc8b43b64b5cb7fa17c3af868a88
msgid ""
"**Setup.** A repo-level refactor renames `cmd/sync/main.go` to `cmd/sync-"
"tool/main.go` and simultaneously splits the old `runSync` function into "
"`runSync` and `runSyncBatch`. Three pages cite the old path:"
msgstr ""
"**背景设定。** 一次仓库级重构把 `cmd/sync/main.go` 重命名为 `cmd/sync-tool/main.go`，同时把旧的 "
"`runSync` 函数拆成 `runSync` 和 `runSyncBatch`。三个页面引用了旧路径："

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:160
#: 0d4ee3ddab5e492fb8707b218776d6d2
msgid "`repo-map.md` — auto-generated; just needs regeneration."
msgstr "`repo-map.md` —— 自动生成；只需要重新生成一次。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:161
#: 637ae3f64a1f40cd9a36e929021418e4
msgid ""
"`runbook.md` — one paragraph says \"run `cmd/sync/main.go`\"; the rest of "
"the page is fine."
msgstr "`runbook.md` —— 其中一段写着“run `cmd/sync/main.go`”；页面其余部分一切正常。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:163
#: 4b2bac43589a4790906a2384cfe19988
msgid ""
"`architecture.md` — two paragraphs explain *why* `runSync` was structured "
"the way it was; the split is a structural change."
msgstr ""
"`architecture.md` —— 其中两段解释了 * 为什么 * `runSync` 以那种方式组织起来；这次拆分是一次结构性变更。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:166
#: bf85700a8e9844808ec8f331ae97fdc4
msgid ""
"**Sync (Chapter 14).** L-git and L-link both flag all three pages. L-entity "
"flags `runbook.md` and `architecture.md` (both cite the function whose "
"entity ID changed when the file moved and split)."
msgstr ""
"**同步（第 14 章）。** L-git 和 L-link 都把这三页全都标了出来。L-entity 标了 `runbook.md` 和 "
"`architecture.md`（两者都引用了“因文件被移动和拆分而实体 ID 已变”的那个函数）。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:170
#: 81737978db1d4b8e977d61e6c502f75b
msgid "**Dispatcher.**"
msgstr "**派发器。**"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:172
#: 7e82cb0b069044a9af5a6acf5a13c0f8
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`repo-map.md`: path is in `{repo-map.md, api-reference.md}` → "
"**L1_REGENERATE.**"
msgstr ""
"`repo-map.md`：路径在 `{repo-map.md, api-reference.md}` 中 → **L1_REGENERATE。**"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:174
#: faa832c1129042a9936a85bdf1876407
msgid ""
"`runbook.md`: path is not in any policy-override set. Tags include L-link; "
"is the link target still a file that exists? Yes — `cmd/sync-tool/main.go` "
"exists. **L1_FIX_LINK.**"
msgstr ""
"`runbook.md`：路径不在任何策略覆盖集合中。标签里包括 L-link；链接目标是否仍然是一个存在的文件？是的 —— `cmd/sync-"
"tool/main.go` 存在。 **L1_FIX_LINK。**"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:177
#: ff01f961a31a41f59c9cd5785781c376
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`architecture.md`: path is in `{architecture/}` → **L3** immediately. The "
"dispatcher does not even inspect the tags."
msgstr "`architecture.md`：路径在 `{architecture/}` 中 → 立即走 **L3** 。派发器根本不会去看标签。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:180
#: f75d400e4b814007b1a1b79fd722054d
msgid "**Execution.**"
msgstr "**执行。**"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:182
#: 87fea9127f6543c9ba955cd1ce6fd1e3
msgid ""
"L1 regenerates `repo-map.md` from `git ls-files` (zero tokens, "
"deterministic)."
msgstr "L1 用 `git ls-files` 重新生成 `repo-map.md`（零 token，确定性）。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:184
#: 43c082b3bdf841c9b15fc731d1af6cba
msgid ""
"L1 rewrites the one link in `runbook.md` from `cmd/sync/main.go` to "
"`cmd/sync-tool/main.go` (zero tokens, localised edit)."
msgstr ""
"L1 把 `runbook.md` 里那一条链接从 `cmd/sync/main.go` 重写为 `cmd/sync-tool/main.go`（零 "
"token，局部编辑）。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:187
#: 0acc1099d12049eba5d668c6aec5bc28
msgid ""
"L3 opens a human-reviewable task: *\"`architecture.md` cites `runSync`, "
"which has been split. Does the architectural explanation in §3 need "
"rewriting, or just a sentence about the new `runSyncBatch`? Please "
"review.\"* A human decides; an ADR may follow; the LLM is involved only if "
"the human asks."
msgstr ""
"L3 开出一个可由人评审的任务： * “`architecture.md` 引用了 `runSync`，而它已被拆分。§3 "
"里那段架构解释是需要整段重写，还是只需要加一句关于新 `runSyncBatch` 的说明？请评审。” * 由人做决定；可能随后产出一份 "
"ADR；只有当人主动要求时，LLM 才会介入。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:193
#: 0a977c4d696547dc8c5f4b3ea25e7050
msgid ""
"**Gate run (Chapter 15).** After L1 and L3 complete, the publish gates run "
"across all three pages. H4 (citations resolve) and H5 (links resolve) both "
"pass now. H1/H2/H3 (footer shape) pass for L1's footers because the scripts "
"wrote them correctly; pass for `architecture.md` because the human "
"remembered to update the footer along with the body."
msgstr ""
"**门禁跑动（第 15 章）。** L1 和 L3 做完之后，发布门禁会对这三页都跑一遍。H4（引用可解析）和 "
"H5（链接可解析）现在都通过。H1/H2/H3（footer 形状）对 L1 的 footer 都通过，因为脚本本来就写对了；对 "
"`architecture.md` 也通过，因为那位人类记得在改正文的同时把 footer 一起更新。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:200
#: c3bcc636cc4c4c16b13d4a36b5e33887
msgid ""
"**Cost audit.** LLM calls: zero for L1; none for L3 unless the human invoked"
" one. Human review scope: one page (`architecture.md`), which is a genuinely"
" structural change and *deserves* human attention. Compare with the naive "
"baseline (\"regenerate every page that mentions `runSync`\"), which would "
"have produced three LLM-generated diffs for the reviewer to wade through, "
"two of which should never have been generated."
msgstr ""
"**成本审计。** LLM 调用次数：L1 为零；L3 "
"为零，除非人类主动调了一次。人工评审范围：一个页面（`architecture.md`），而那确实是一次结构性变更， * 本来就该 * "
"交给人。与朴素基线（“对每一个提到 `runSync` 的页面都重新生成”）对比一下：那种做法会产出三份 LLM 生成的 diff "
"给评审者去蹚，其中两份本来就 * 不该被生成 * 。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:208
#: 19dd6998486b4bf398fde534434374a6
msgid "Why \"rule first\" beats \"LLM first\""
msgstr "为什么“rule first”胜过“LLM first”"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:210
#: 09fcc1ce967645be8a880c2eb5aabfe5
msgid ""
"It is tempting, with cheap LLMs, to skip L1 entirely and hand every "
"candidate to L2. Do not. Three reasons, in decreasing order of importance:"
msgstr "在 LLM 变便宜以后，很容易想完全跳过 L1、把每一个候选都扔给 L2。不要这么干。按重要性递减排三个理由："

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:214
#: db70a642c06549048251e5591e686741
msgid ""
"**Human attention.** Every LLM call produces a diff a human reviews. Ten L1 "
"wins a week is ten reviews saved. One hundred is 100."
msgstr ""
"**人类注意力。** 每一次 LLM 调用都会产出一份要被人评审的 diff。一周十次 L1 命中 = 十次被省下来的评审。一百次就是 100 次。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:217
#: ca7a4c371929471ca1137758ddaad398
msgid ""
"**Determinism.** L1 rules have the same answer every time. L2 does not — the"
" same prompt with the same model at temperature 0 can produce subtly "
"different prose on different days as models are upgraded. For anything a "
"rule can handle, having the rule be the source of truth is more stable."
msgstr ""
"**确定性。** L1 规则每次给出的答案都相同。L2 不会 —— 同一段提示词、同一个模型、temperature "
"0，也可能因为模型在不断升级，在不同日子产出略有差别的文字。凡是规则能搞定的事，把规则作为 source of truth 更稳定。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:222
#: eeb23ff2e751419f9d605bd2e326a726
msgid ""
"**Privacy.** L1 runs entirely on local filesystem and git. L2 sends page "
"content, diffs, and prompts to a model provider. Chapter 22 unpacks the "
"privacy implications; suffice it to say here that a rule-first discipline "
"reduces the surface area of things sent to third parties, simply by handling"
" more cases before the LLM is consulted."
msgstr ""
"**隐私。** L1 完全跑在本地文件系统和 git 上。L2 会把页面内容、diff 和提示词发给模型提供方。第 22 "
"章会把隐私方面的影响讲透；这里只需要说一句：rule-first 纪律会让更多案例在调 LLM "
"之前就被处理掉，从而直接缩小“发给第三方的东西”的表面积。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:229
#: 108b52218b104e589c19136f29d4725a
msgid "When L2 is the right choice"
msgstr "什么时候 L2 才是正确选择"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:231
#: f400c71bf6a246cb9d9348be7bee2b34
msgid ""
"L2 is for the case that genuinely exists between L1 (too mechanical) and L3 "
"(too structural): a localised content change where an LLM can do, in a few "
"thousand tokens, what a human would do in ten minutes but with a higher per-"
"minute cost. Function renames, type-signature changes, parameter additions, "
"documentation for a straightforwardly new helper function — these all land "
"cleanly in L2 because a human reviewer can verify the one-paragraph diff "
"quickly."
msgstr ""
"L2 对应那种确确实实落在 L1（太机械）和 L3（太结构性）之间的情形：一次局部的内容变更 —— LLM 用几千 token "
"就能做的事，人要花十分钟、而且每分钟成本更高。函数重命名、类型签名变更、加一个参数、为一个明显新增的 helper 函数补文档 —— 这些都能干净地落在"
" L2，因为人类评审者可以很快核对一份一段长度的 diff。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:239
#: a1218411508f41a8b2e1a1d3a6a44540
msgid ""
"L2 is *not* for cross-page consistency (the LLM does not see the other "
"pages), not for architectural rewrites (not enough context), and not for new"
" content (there is no \"page to patch\"). Putting those cases through L2 "
"produces plausible-looking output that a reviewer has to correct anyway, so "
"nothing is gained."
msgstr ""
"L2 * 不 * 适合做跨页一致性（LLM "
"看不到别的页面），不适合做架构性重写（上下文不够），也不适合做“从零的新内容”（根本没有“被打补丁的页面”）。把这些情形塞进 "
"L2，只会产出看起来像样、但评审者反正都得改一遍的输出，等于什么都没赚到。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:245
#: 8e6b53fab15341bba36b393b2db6476d
msgid "Example"
msgstr "Example —— 范例"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:247
#: 16611eda11fc49b88cc38810208262f0
msgid ""
"A week of real operation, summarised as a batch report — the kind of output "
"a Friday-afternoon digest posts to the team's channel:"
msgstr "真实运营一周之后，汇总为一份批量报告 —— 周五下午推送到团队频道的那种摘要："

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:269
#: 86ff5bb5fc2746fc89ffcad3f946d107
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Two points of interest. First, L1 handled 63% of the week's candidates for "
"zero cost. Second, the reviewer's queue was two items — both genuinely "
"requiring human thought — not nineteen. That ratio, not the token cost, is "
"the metric the operational model actually optimises for."
msgstr ""
"有两点值得留意。其一，L1 以零成本处理掉了这一周 63% 的候选。其二，评审者的队列里只有两项 —— 两项都是真的需要人去想的 —— "
"而不是十九项。这个比例，而不是 token 成本，才是运维模型真正在优化的指标。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:275
#: aee2648bda1d45a5bb34123ccba19671
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr "Conclusion —— 小结"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:277
#: ff1625d7829045cdb982f79da05645af
msgid ""
"Maintenance is not a single problem; it is three problems pretending to be "
"one. L1 is a filesystem-and-git problem. L2 is an LLM problem with bounded "
"context. L3 is a human problem that the machinery should stay out of. "
"Routing correctly between them — rule first, LLM second, human for "
"structural change — is what makes a KB sustainable as the code beneath it "
"accelerates."
msgstr ""
"维护不是一个问题；它是三个“伪装成一个”的问题。L1 是一个文件系统与 git 的问题。L2 是一个上下文受限的 LLM 问题。L3 "
"是一个“机器应当退开”的人类问题。在这三者之间做正确的路由 —— rule first、LLM second、人来管结构性变更 —— "
"就是让一个知识库在它脚下的代码加速时仍然可持续的关键。"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:284
#: 03869983a31e49e18b86a579b8e24fea
msgid ""
"Part IV's three chapters have now laid out the whole loop: detect candidates"
" (ch14), check them against hard and soft gates (ch15), dispatch them "
"through the three levels (ch16). The next two parts (V and VI) put this loop"
" to work: Chapter 18 uses the footer's review state as the fourth axis of "
"document layering, and Chapter 21 asks what happens when an agent — not a "
"human — consumes the output."
msgstr ""
"至此，第四部分的三章已经铺出了整条回路：检测候选（第 14 章）、用硬软门禁检验它们（第 15 章）、把它们经由三级派发出去（第 16 "
"章）。接下来的两部分（V 和 VI）会让这条回路真正运转起来：第 18 章会把 footer 的评审状态作为文档分层的第四根轴；第 21 "
"章会问：当“消费输出”的不是人、而是一个 agent 时，会发生什么？"

#: ../../part4-operations-lifecycle/ch16-maintenance-drift-and-link-rot.md:291
#: df029d3802784b66978596764e4178c5
